# Braintrust CLI-generated local state
.bt/
.corvus/
.eval-checkpoints/
# Legacy locations used before Corvus runtime state was consolidated.
.corvus-rate-limits/
.corvus-collector.lock
# Collected data stays local. Data cards are documentation, not data: they
# record collection scope and yield with no source text, and the README links
# to them. Git will not descend into an ignored directory, so the directories
# themselves must be un-ignored before the card can be excepted.
data/corvus_live/**
!data/corvus_live/**/
!data/corvus_live/*/README.md

# Frozen benchmark artifacts are gold answers. The source policy releases only
# derived facts and source URLs AND requires legal review before publication, so
# committing a freeze to git would publish it ahead of that review. Same
# treatment as collected data: the card is documentation, the artifact is not.
curation/**
!curation/**/
!curation/*/README.md

# Analysis inputs. The JSONL files are Braintrust experiment dumps carrying model
# answers and benchmark rows under the upstream LiveNewsBench canary, and the
# row-level CSVs are the same data reshaped. Summary tables, figures, and the
# written reports are committed, because those are the analysis. Regenerate the
# inputs with export_braintrust_results.py.
analysis/*.jsonl
analysis/variable_row_level.csv
analysis/context_timing_rows.csv

# Hugging Face release artifact. Rebuild with analysis/build_hf_dataset.py. The
# published copy is gated on the Hub, so committing it here would route around
# the gate.
hf_dataset/

# Rendered deliverables and local scratch
output/
tmp/

# Editor and operating-system files
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
